course: dictionary
lesson: 5576
title: Leukaemia: a cancer of the blood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Leukaemia is a kind of cancer. It starts in the blood and in the bone marrow, the soft inside part of bones where new blood cells are made.
explain: Blood contains white cells that fight germs. In leukaemia, the body makes too many faulty white blood cells, and they crowd out the healthy ones. «In Birmingham, Precious's brother has leukaemia, a blood cancer, and is in hospital for months.» The words after the comma explain the word for you.
explain: Leukaemia cannot be caught like a cold. «Leukaemia is a kind of blood cancer; it cannot be caught from another person.» So a classmate with leukaemia is not a risk to you in that way.
fact: Leukaemia is a kind of cancer of the blood and bone marrow.
fact: Bone marrow is the soft part inside bones where new blood cells are made.
fact: Leukaemia cannot be caught from another person, like a cold.
fact: Treatment such as chemotherapy can help many people with leukaemia get better.
fact: «Childhood leukaemia» means leukaemia in children, and charities raise money for research into it.
exercise: Leukaemia is a kind of what? | *cancer of the blood and bone marrow | a broken bone | a cold caught from a classmate | a type of food
exercise: Can leukaemia be caught from another person? | *No, it cannot be caught like a cold | Yes, by sharing drinks | Yes, if you sit near someone for a long time | Only in winter
exercise: «It can make hair fall out for a while, which usually grows back.» What does for a while mean? | Just on Tuesdays | Until the hair is cut | *For a short time | For ever
test: Where does leukaemia begin in the body? | In the ears | In the stomach | *In the blood and bone marrow | Only in the lungs
test: In leukaemia, what does the body make too many of? | Bones | Germs | *Faulty white blood cells | Healthy red sweets
exam: Why can a child with leukaemia sit next to you safely in class? | Because they never feel unwell | Because they have finished all their treatment for ever | *Because leukaemia cannot be caught from another person | Because leukaemia only affects adults
